 "explanation": {
  "state": "check",
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified VAI 413 days after the shortage posting",
  "sentences": [
   {
    "text": "FDA's shortage list shows ibutilide fumarate has been in shortage since 2022-04-29 and remains listed as of 2026-10-21, a duration of 54 months.",
    "cites": [
     "D5"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "The product label identifies Pharmacia & Upjohn Company LLC (FEI 1810189) as the manufacturing plant for the NDC in use.",
    "cites": [
     "E11"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "That plant received a VAI classification from its most recent inspection ending 2023-06-16, with the classification letter issued 2024-09-10 — 413 days after the shortage posting.",
    "cites": [
     "D3",
     "E10"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Prior inspections of the same plant in 2009, 2010, 2011, 2012, 2013, 2015, and 2018 were also classified VAI.",
    "cites": [
     "E3",
     "E4",
     "E5",
     "E6",
     "E7",
     "E8",
     "E9"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "Corvale General holds 54 units at 4.5 per day (12 days on hand) and Corvale Lakeside holds 12 units at 1 per day (12 days on hand).",
    "cites": [
     "D1",
     "D2"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "The rule‑based alternate is Heritage Pharmaceuticals Inc. d/b/a Avet Pharmaceuticals Inc., which is not on FDA's shortage list today, though its label names no plant we could place.",
    "cites": [
     "D4"
    ]
   }
  ],
